  m_Name: Scene10_FAQ_1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OhmsLaw.DialogueLine
  id: Scene10_FAQ_1
  speaker: WATTSON
  text: Starting low is good detective practice. A small push gives a small, safe
    current, we can check that everything is connected properly, and then we raise
    the voltage one step at a time so we can see clearly what each step does to the
    current.
